Commit:     totalwindupflightsystems <totalwindupflightsystems@gmail.com>
CommitDate: Sun Sep 20 08:59:55 2026 -0500

    fix(embedding): OPS-008 pool on-the-fly cache-miss embeds
    
    semanticSearch walked candidates in a serial for-loop and awaited each
    cache miss one text at a time, so a cold-cache slice cost
    `misses x provider RTT`. Measured live on a quiet host (load ~4):
    direct OpenRouter /v1/embeddings for qwen/qwen3-embedding-8b answered in
    2.3-7.6s (healthy), while the daemon's authed ?q= took 32.6/39.5/32.7s and
    still 27.7s on a repeated query. With maxOnTheFlyEmbeds=10 (recall.ts) the
    serial sum was 10 x RTT = 23-76s, which is the measured band and the source
    of the "Semantic search timed out after 30s" 500s.
    
    Split the scan into cache-resolve, then embed the miss set through a bounded
    worker pool (the rebuild.ts shape, default 4, clamped >= 1), then rank.
    Misses are deduped by content hash so repeated embedding_text still issues
    one request, and the cap counts unique misses. A failing embed is contained
    per text: it stays unranked and uncached, siblings in flight are unaffected.
    Scoring stays outside the pool so cosineSimilarity's empty-vector guard
    still surfaces. Warm-cache ranking, minScore floor, sort order and
    cachedOnly semantics are unchanged.
    
    Regression suite (10 tests) proves RED on the old serial code (maxInFlight=1,
    804ms for 8 misses at 100ms RTT) and green after: max in-flight > 1 and
    <= concurrency, cap honored exactly, dedupe, failure isolation, cachedOnly
    issues zero calls, and pooled wall time tracks ceil(misses/concurrency) x RTT.
    
    Gates: 160 files / 1275 tests pass, tsc clean, prettier clean.
    
    Addresses OPS-008.
    
    Co-authored-by: Alexis Okuwa <wojonstech@gmail.com>
